Things that I think I am going to need if I want to use this compiler:
 - builtins that will be needed such as chr(), ord(), int(), hex(), min(), max()

Things that would be nice to have for convenience:
 - import statements for supporting inter-module variables and functions.
 - function default parameter support.
 - function keyword argument support.
 - asm() block to allow inlining assembly.
 - auto-infer types for variables that can be inferred.
 - walrus operator.

Optimizations that would be nice to have:
 - load/store purpose tracking, so redundant loads/stores and moves can be tracked.
 - optimization passes for unnecessary store/load and side-by-side addpci/subpci calls (many such cases), comparison against const is one.
 - optimization passes for memcpy_unrolled for direction of copy in case we're already sitting on a value (add16 test case).
 - find JRI/LNGJUMP that points at the next instruction and remove it.
 - duplicate instruction chain finder, replace with LNGJUMP to save on space.
 - replace LNGJUMP with JRI when appropriately small jumps exist.
 - non-const string initialization to "" shouldn't call strcpy.
 - two lines of "SWAP PC, SPC" in a row.
 - look for booleans that get calculated out only to be "INV" for a JRI or LNGJUMP.

Things that would be good for a complete compiler that I probably will not need:
 - 8/16/32 bit signed division.
 - 8/16/32 bit signed modulo.
 - 8/16/32 bit exponentiation.
 - variable pointer support.
 - function pointer support.
 - integer/boolean array support, including reading/writing values using array syntax.
 - support for allocating local and global arrays using int[length].
 - support for allocating extern global arrays using int[inf] or similar syntax.
